Keywords: metal-organic frameworks • conjugated mesoporous polymers • nanoparticles • hydrophobicity • hydrogenation
We synthesized a series of MIL101@Pt@FeP-CMP coating with hydrophobic and porous shell. In the hydrogenation of cinnamaldehyde, FeP-CMP shell not only maintains selectivity with the help of iron(III) porphyrin but also promotes catalytic efficiency due to the environmental hydrophobicity. Especially, MIL101@Pt@FeP-CMP\(^{\text{sponge}}\) catalyst reached the highest TOF (1516.1 h\(^{-1}\)) and outperformed state-of-the-art catalysts.
